{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: the original model computed the Gaussian-process covariance using parameters `alpha`, `rho`, and `sigma` before their prior sampling statements. SafeStan requires each parameter to be observed with its unique prior before any model-block use. The rewritten model declares the local matrices first, then applies the three existing built-in priors, then computes the covariance and scores `y` with the same `multi_normal_cholesky` likelihood. No data changes were required.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] real x;
  vector[N] y;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> rho;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}
model {
  matrix[N, N] cov;
  matrix[N, N] L_cov;

  rho ~ gamma(25, 4);
  alpha ~ normal(0, 2);
  sigma ~ normal(0, 1);

  cov = gp_exp_quad_cov(x, alpha, rho)
        + diag_matrix(rep_vector(sigma, N));
  L_cov = cholesky_decompose(cov);

  y ~ multi_normal_cholesky(rep_vector(0, N), L_cov);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":5,"x":[3.642731488698852,5.01230000847379,5.057660038827569,4.37480121700133,3.983777384057646],"y":[4.0,5.0,5.0,4.0,4.0]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
